<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <Description>The resource audit every feature's suite runs over its own shared string resources: each neutral key is one the composed model derives by convention or one the source spells as a string literal, and each satellite key is one its neutral file declares. Reads .resx files and source text alone, so it references nothing beyond the base class library.</Description>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- The test-tree props add a global `using Xunit` for every project under test/. This one is
         plumbing rather than a suite and references no test framework at all, so the global using
         would not compile. -->
    <Using Remove="Xunit" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- No references of any kind: the audit reads files, so any suite, of Core, of a pack or of a
       distribution, references it without taking a second copy of anything. Omitting
       Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk keeps IsTestProject false, so `dotnet test Tellma.slnx` never tries to
       run this project. -->

</Project>
